615:flutter pub add freerasp:8.2.4   # exactly the version the template was checked against
671:`FreeRaspServiceImpl` forwards **every** detection freerasp 8.2.4 reports - the exact version step 1 adds, and the only one the adapter was checked against. Moving to another version means re-checking `ThreatCallback`, as below. Each freeRASP `Threat` reaches `onThreatDetected` as the `SecurityThreat` below, and malware, which freeRASP delivers on its own callback rather than as a `Threat`, arrives as `SecurityThreat.malware`. No detection is deliberately ignored. Once only 10 of the 23 callbacks were set, and freeRASP drops a detection whose callback is null without logging it.
703:That guard covers new `Threat` values **only**. freeRASP also delivers some detections on a callback of their own (`onMalware` is one), and every `ThreatCallback` parameter is optional: a version that adds such a callback still compiles with the adapter leaving it null, and freeRASP then drops that detection without logging it. On every freerasp upgrade, compare `ThreatCallback`'s parameters with the ones `_start()` passes, by hand.
